@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@using UBookIt.Web.Theming
@inject IOptions<UBookItThemeOptions> UBookItTheme
@*
    The only route by which uBookIt emits its own styling.

    A consuming site opts in with one line in the head of its layout, rendering
    this partial by its path: ~/Views/Shared/UBookIt/_Styles.cshtml

    Three reasons it is a partial rather than a link element the site writes itself.

    Head placement. The flows render from ViewComponents, and a ViewComponent
    cannot contribute to the document head — a Razor section does not cross that
    boundary, the same boundary that makes ModelState unavailable to the flow and
    forced the TempData workaround. So a stylesheet emitted from inside a flow
    could only ever be a link in the body, which buys a flash of unstyled content
    on the very surface that has no JavaScript to hide it.

    Cascade order. The package's defaults must come before the site's overrides,
    and that ordering is a property of where this partial sits rather than
    something a token can express. Sites are documented to link their own
    stylesheet after this one.

    A theme's off-switch — now built, and it is the condition below. A theme owns
    the markup, so the package's classes largely do not exist in the rendered
    document: the stylesheet would style nothing while still being able to collide
    with the theme's own. A theme that reuses the package's shared partials as
    building blocks registers with usePackageStylesheet: true and gets back exactly
    what an unthemed site gets. That is why the requirement is that this be the ONLY
    emission route: a second link element somewhere else would survive the theme and
    fight it.

    IOptions rather than the theme object itself, because this partial renders in
    hosts that never registered a theme — including the package's own rendering rig.
    IOptions<T> always resolves, and no theme is simply the default value.

    Two notes for anyone editing this file.

    Razor comments do NOT nest. An inner comment closes this one early and everything
    below becomes live markup, which is how the first version of this file failed to
    compile.

    The link element below sits at column 0 inside the block ON PURPOSE. Razor emits
    literal markup including its leading whitespace, so indenting it to match the
    braces changes the bytes an unthemed site renders — which was verified against the
    running TestSite, and which is the one thing this change promised not to do.
*@
@if (!UBookItTheme.Value.IsActive || UBookItTheme.Value.UsePackageStylesheet)
{
<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/_content/UBookIt.Web/ubookit.css" />
}
